From f5e9356b7b0416e2fa147f1d160ec888a547f62f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Himess <semihcvlk53@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:27:30 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] feat(shared): Profile H verifier hygiene in
 user-decryption-signature (lifecycle Level 1)

Adds profile_h.rs, the Profile H rules of the Decryption Authority
Lifecycle draft for the RFC-012/016 signature check, as a new entry point
(verify_user_decryption_signature); verify_signature is left unchanged:

- H1: signature, public key and extra-data caps (64 KiB / 4 KiB / 1 KiB by
  default) checked before any host-chain read; a violation is final.
- H2: code-first ordering at one pinned block B (eth_getCode and the
  isValidSignature call both at B, nothing cached across verifications):
  empty code -> 65-byte ecrecover only; an exact 23-byte EIP-7702
  delegation indicator -> ERC-1271, with an ecrecover fallback only when
  the call succeeded with empty return data and the signature is 65 bytes
  (never on a revert, including an empty one); other code -> ERC-1271 only.
- H3: gas limit B_exec + 21,000 + 64 x len(calldata), B_exec = 2,000,000.
- H4: at most two ERC-1271 negatives per request, a block apart; the caller
  carries the AttemptState between processing attempts.
- H8: off | shadow | enforce; shadow serves the off verdict and reports
  the code-first one next to it, sharing a single isValidSignature call.

lib.rs: new Erc1271Error variants (CapExceeded, EmptyReturn,
AwaitingNextBlock, AttemptsExhausted), the call-error mapping factored into
map_erc1271_call_error, re-exports. Drafted by a delegated agent, reviewed
line by line against the draft and formatted with rustfmt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
